<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prussian Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1217–1274</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades">Northern Crusades</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prussian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> was the series of thirteenth-century campaigns by Polish dukes and above all the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> to conquer and Christianise the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-prussians">Old Prussians</a> on the south-eastern Baltic coast. The Teutonic Knights arrived in the 1230s and built castles such as Thorn and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konigsberg">Königsberg</a>. After crushing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a> by 1274, they made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> the base of their state.</p></div>
